  table  -> /root/rna_work_r/results/tables/x4_mbased_vs_binomial.tsv

=== verdict ===
Per-sample ASE rate against miscall rate: rho = 0.949  p = 2.44e-06
Significant genes carry a lowest alternate fraction of 0.0769 against 0.4286 for the rest.

Both predictions of the genotyping hypothesis hold. The imbalance MBASED reports is a property of the variant calls, not of allelic
regulation, and it cannot be filtered away: the genotypes were derived from the same reads the expression is measured in, so any
filter that removes the doubtful calls also removes the evidence. ASE is NOT assessable on this dataset - the same verdict the
upstream pipeline reached, now reproduced by a second method with a different statistical model.

Assessing it properly needs genotypes from an orthogonal source: DNA from the same individuals, or at minimum an external panel.

=== x4 done ===
